{"h": {"measure": "A", "k": 20}, "sp": "nb", "rep": 101, "hyps": [{"edit_edge": 3, "edit_op": "skip_connect", "cond_edge": 3, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "higher", "why": "Adding a direct input-to-output skip where the edge was missing restores a path and helps more than replacing an existing conv/op on that edge."}, {"edit_edge": 4, "edit_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "cond_edge": 3, "cond_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "direction": "lower", "why": "When edge 3 already holds a strong 3x3 conv, the extra conv on edge 4 yields diminishing returns (+0.7 vs +2.2/+1.5 in experiments 1-3)."}, {"edit_edge": 4, "edit_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "cond_edge": 4, "cond_op": "avg_pool_3x3", "direction": "higher", "why": "Replacing a weak avg_pool with a 3x3 conv gives a large gain on all datasets."}, {"edit_edge": 5, "edit_op": "none", "cond_edge": 3, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "lower", "why": "With edge 3 absent, edge 5 is a main route to the output, so removing it hurts more (C100 -4.68 vs -2.30)."}, {"edit_edge": 3, "edit_op": "skip_connect", "cond_edge": 5, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "higher", "why": "When the other output edges are none, adding a skip on edge 3 reconnects input to output, giving a huge gain (experiment 10)."}, {"edit_edge": 0, "edit_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "cond_edge": 0, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "higher", "why": "Replacing a missing first edge with a 3x3 conv gains more than upgrading an existing skip or pool."}, {"edit_edge": 1, "edit_op": "avg_pool_3x3", "cond_edge": 1, "cond_op": "skip_connect", "direction": "higher", "why": "Swapping a skip for a pool costs less than replacing a 1x1 conv with pooling (experiments 12-14)."}, {"edit_edge": 5, "edit_op": "nor_conv_1x1", "cond_edge": 5, "cond_op": "skip_connect", "direction": "higher", "why": "Replacing the output skip with a conv is generally beneficial when the rest of the cell is conv-rich, and more so when edge 1 is not skip."}, {"edit_edge": 2, "edit_op": "skip_connect", "cond_edge": 2, "cond_op": "none", "